#: src/libvlc-module.c:174
msgid "Efficient resampling"
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:176
msgid ""
"Use the lightweight band-limited Speex resampler for audio/video clock-drift "
"correction instead of libsamplerate's costlier SINC. The drift ratio stays "
"close to 1.0, so SINC buys no audible quality but eats several percent of a "
"CPU core on older Macs. This only affects drift correction; fixed sample-"
"rate conversion for music (e.g. 44.1 to 48 kHz) is left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:183
#, fuzzy
msgid "Lightweight A/52 (AC-3) decoder"
msgstr "كاشف الرموز السمعي ATSC A/52 (AC-3)"

#: src/libvlc-module.c:185
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Decode Dolby Digital (A/52) with liba52 instead of libavcodec. Measured on "
"an iBook G3 600 MHz playing a DVD: 68.9 %% of the CPU against 72.3 %% for "
"libavcodec, i.e. about 3.5 points cheaper, AND decoding in floating point "
"where libavcodec falls back to its fixed-point variant on CPUs without SIMD "
"-- so this is both faster and more accurate there. Machines with AltiVec/SSE "
"keep libavcodec, whose vectorised paths cost them nothing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libvlc-module.c:194
msgid ""
